              "a11yRetry": "Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again.",
              "textField": "Our blood pressure medicines will target the most important factors that are involved in blood pressure regulation. Those include *heart rate* or in other words, the beats per minute, *stroke volume* or in other words the amount of blood that is ejected in each beat, and the *diameter of the arterioles*. The *autonomic nervous system* plays the biggest role in heart rate physiologically, so we use drugs of that system to affect heart rate, but it can also play a role in stroke volume, as the strength of the contraction of the heart is affected by that system. The *volume of fluid* is important in stroke volume, and as such, our diuretics will attempt to address that factor. Finally, the diameter of the arterioles is under the control of the autonomic nervous system, angiotensin, and *nitric oxide* as well as other mediators, and therefore some of our medications will aim to mimic or block the effects of those natural substances. It is not uncommon for a client to be on a combination of drugs that target all of the three most important factors involved in blood pressure regulation."
            },
